# Project Context

This project is a Brazilian application for a teacher to manage students, classes, attendance, make-up lessons, payments, and financial information.

## Sources of truth

The project has two primary reference documents:

- `.cursor/docs/overview.md` — source of truth for product behavior, functional flows, business rules, states, validations, and user interactions.
- `.cursor/docs/software-architecture.md` — source of truth for technical structure, architecture, stack, engineering conventions, testing strategy, and local infrastructure.

Use the appropriate document instead of guessing.

## Mandatory principles

- Never invent product behavior that is not supported by `overview.md`.
- Never use the architecture document to redefine business rules.
- When product behavior is unclear, inspect `overview.md` before implementing.
- When technical structure is unclear, inspect `software-architecture.md` before introducing a new pattern.
- Preserve existing decisions unless there is a concrete inconsistency.
- Do not introduce authentication, authorization, roles, or permissions unless they become part of the defined product scope.
- Keep the implementation aligned with the documented scope.
- Future features explicitly marked as out of scope must not be implemented proactively.

## Language conventions

- Product/domain documentation may remain in Portuguese because the application targets a Brazilian context.
- Source code, identifiers, and technical conventions should use English.
- User-facing text should follow the product language and the requirements defined in the functional documentation.
